1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,407
A ball rolls down a slope
and up the other side.

2
00:00:03,407 --> 00:00:06,230
A child on a slide speeds
up on the way down.

3
00:00:06,630 --> 00:00:07,912
Speed comes and goes.

4
00:00:07,912 --> 00:00:10,534
Where does it go, and
how does it come back?

5
00:00:10,984 --> 00:00:13,822
Diya pulls her little cousin's
swing back, and lets go.

6
00:00:14,172 --> 00:00:18,082
It speeds up, slows down, stops
for a moment, and comes back.

7
00:00:18,082 --> 00:00:19,240
Nobody pushes it.

8
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:20,589
What keeps it going?

9
00:00:21,089 --> 00:00:25,703
By the end of this video, you will
predict its speed with one simple rule.

10
00:00:26,353 --> 00:00:28,328
So what is mechanical energy?

11
00:00:28,678 --> 00:00:30,024
It has two parts.

12
00:00:30,024 --> 00:00:33,117
Kinetic energy, K, is
the energy of motion.

13
00:00:33,517 --> 00:00:38,427
Potential energy, U, is energy stored
by height, or in a stretched spring.

14
00:00:38,827 --> 00:00:42,044
Add them, and you get
the mechanical energy, E.

15
00:00:42,044 --> 00:00:43,441
E equals K plus U.

16
00:00:43,841 --> 00:00:49,025
The rule: if only conservative forces
like gravity do work, E never changes.

17
00:00:49,025 --> 00:00:50,674
K and U trade places.

18
00:00:51,324 --> 00:00:52,239
Let's run it.

19
00:00:52,239 --> 00:00:56,262
A twenty kilogram child on a swing,
two point five metres long, pulled

20
00:00:56,262 --> 00:00:57,675
back to sixty degrees.

21
00:00:58,025 --> 00:01:01,735
At the top, the seat is one
point two five metres up.

22
00:01:01,735 --> 00:01:04,408
U is two hundred and forty five joules.

23
00:01:04,408 --> 00:01:05,335
K is zero.

24
00:01:05,735 --> 00:01:06,635
Let go.

25
00:01:06,538 --> 00:01:09,706
As it swings down, U falls and K rises.

26
00:01:10,106 --> 00:01:14,863
At the bottom, U is zero, and K is
the full two hundred and forty five

27
00:01:14,863 --> 00:01:15,763
joules.

28
00:01:15,529 --> 00:01:18,064
Speed: about five metres per second.

29
00:01:18,464 --> 00:01:21,064
Up the other side, K turns back into U.

30
00:01:21,064 --> 00:01:23,802
It stops at the same
height it started from.

31
00:01:24,302 --> 00:01:28,974
On the graph, U and K rise and fall,
but their sum, E, is a flat line.

32
00:01:29,624 --> 00:01:31,624
Slow-mo replay, near the bottom.

33
00:01:31,974 --> 00:01:36,346
The rope pulls at right angles to
the motion, so it does no work.

34
00:01:36,346 --> 00:01:38,414
Only gravity changes the speed.

35
00:01:39,064 --> 00:01:40,820
Now the proof, step by step.

36
00:01:41,170 --> 00:01:42,070
Step one.

37
00:01:41,984 --> 00:01:43,663
The work energy theorem.

38
00:01:43,663 --> 00:01:47,606
The work done on a body equals
its change in kinetic energy.

39
00:01:48,356 --> 00:01:49,256
Step two.

40
00:01:49,197 --> 00:01:53,732
For a conservative force, the work
equals minus the change in potential

41
00:01:53,732 --> 00:01:54,632
energy.

42
00:01:55,159 --> 00:01:56,138
Step three.

43
00:01:56,138 --> 00:01:58,552
So delta K equals minus delta U.

44
00:01:58,552 --> 00:02:00,413
What K gains, U loses.

45
00:02:01,163 --> 00:02:02,160
Step four.

46
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:04,819
Delta K plus delta U equals zero.

47
00:02:04,819 --> 00:02:07,008
So K plus U never changes.

48
00:02:07,758 --> 00:02:08,663
Step five.

49
00:02:08,663 --> 00:02:13,343
Between any two points, K one plus
U one equals K two plus U two.

50
00:02:14,093 --> 00:02:15,184
Remember this.

51
00:02:15,184 --> 00:02:19,488
With only conservative forces at
work, K plus U stays the same.

52
00:02:20,188 --> 00:02:22,675
So how fast is the seat at the bottom?

53
00:02:22,675 --> 00:02:23,859
Follow the links.

54
00:02:24,209 --> 00:02:25,109
One.

55
00:02:24,797 --> 00:02:27,182
At the top, it is at rest.

56
00:02:27,182 --> 00:02:29,694
All its energy is U, m g h.

57
00:02:30,094 --> 00:02:30,994
Two.

58
00:02:30,620 --> 00:02:32,639
At the bottom, h is zero.

59
00:02:32,639 --> 00:02:35,513
All its energy is K, half m v squared.

60
00:02:35,913 --> 00:02:36,813
Three.

61
00:02:36,566 --> 00:02:39,176
So half m v squared equals m g h.

62
00:02:39,176 --> 00:02:40,546
The mass cancels.

63
00:02:40,946 --> 00:02:41,846
Four.

64
00:02:41,498 --> 00:02:43,184
v equals root two g h.

65
00:02:43,184 --> 00:02:47,099
Root of two times nine point
eight times one point two five.

66
00:02:47,099 --> 00:02:50,038
About four point nine
five metres per second.

67
00:02:50,638 --> 00:02:52,059
Now, side by side.

68
00:02:52,409 --> 00:02:57,047
A twenty kilogram child, and a sixty
kilogram adult, let go from the same

69
00:02:57,047 --> 00:02:57,947
height.

70
00:02:58,093 --> 00:03:01,257
At the bottom, the adult
has three times the energy.

71
00:03:01,257 --> 00:03:03,280
But both move at the same speed.

72
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:04,902
Now you try.

73
00:03:04,902 --> 00:03:09,566
Where is the kinetic energy largest:
at the top of the swing, or at the

74
00:03:09,566 --> 00:03:10,466
bottom?

75
00:03:10,221 --> 00:03:11,491
Pause and decide.

76
00:03:14,691 --> 00:03:15,702
At the bottom!

77
00:03:15,702 --> 00:03:19,532
There the seat is lowest, so U
is smallest, and K is largest.

78
00:03:20,182 --> 00:03:21,082
One more.

79
00:03:20,938 --> 00:03:22,881
A real swing slowly dies down.

80
00:03:22,881 --> 00:03:24,530
Is energy being destroyed?

81
00:03:24,530 --> 00:03:25,663
Pause and think.

82
00:03:28,863 --> 00:03:29,763
No!

83
00:03:29,282 --> 00:03:32,518
Air drag and friction at
the hooks turn it into heat.

84
00:03:32,518 --> 00:03:34,527
The total energy stays the same.

85
00:03:35,177 --> 00:03:36,868
Now, one worked example.

86
00:03:37,218 --> 00:03:42,005
A ball is thrown straight down at three
metres per second, from a ten metre

87
00:03:42,005 --> 00:03:42,905
balcony.

88
00:03:42,713 --> 00:03:44,359
How fast does it land?

89
00:03:44,359 --> 00:03:45,276
Ignore air.

90
00:03:45,776 --> 00:03:49,096
At the top, K one is half
m times three squared.

91
00:03:49,096 --> 00:03:50,868
U one is m g times ten.

92
00:03:51,618 --> 00:03:53,901
At the ground, U two is zero.

93
00:03:53,901 --> 00:03:55,926
K two is half m v squared.

94
00:03:56,676 --> 00:03:58,996
K one plus U one equals K two.

95
00:03:58,996 --> 00:03:59,896
Cancel m.

96
00:03:59,849 --> 00:04:03,957
Four point five, plus ninety
eight, equals half v squared.

97
00:04:04,707 --> 00:04:07,216
So v squared is two hundred and five.

98
00:04:07,216 --> 00:04:10,415
v is about fourteen point
three metres per second.

99
00:04:11,065 --> 00:04:12,527
Now, the exam trap.

100
00:04:12,877 --> 00:04:17,302
Many students use K plus U equals
constant, even when there is friction.

101
00:04:17,652 --> 00:04:20,483
But friction turns some energy into heat.

102
00:04:20,483 --> 00:04:24,958
Then K one plus U one equals K
two plus U two, plus the heat.

103
00:04:25,608 --> 00:04:26,870
Where is this asked?

104
00:04:26,870 --> 00:04:30,081
In speed numericals for swings,
slopes and falling bodies.

105
00:04:30,681 --> 00:04:31,761
Exam level now.

106
00:04:31,761 --> 00:04:35,879
A bob on a one metre string is pulled
aside till the string makes sixty

107
00:04:35,879 --> 00:04:38,322
degrees with the vertical, and let go.

108
00:04:38,322 --> 00:04:41,342
g is ten, cos thirty
seven is zero point eight.

109
00:04:41,342 --> 00:04:45,763
Find its speed when the string makes
thirty seven degrees with the vertical.

110
00:04:45,763 --> 00:04:46,888
Pause and solve.

111
00:04:52,288 --> 00:04:53,606
The answer is A.

112
00:04:53,606 --> 00:04:55,546
Root six metres per second.

113
00:04:56,046 --> 00:04:59,638
It drops L times cos thirty
seven minus cos sixty.

114
00:04:59,638 --> 00:05:01,674
One times zero point three.

115
00:05:01,674 --> 00:05:03,486
Zero point three metres.

116
00:05:03,986 --> 00:05:07,311
Half v squared equals g
times zero point three.

117
00:05:07,311 --> 00:05:11,081
So v squared is two times
ten times zero point three.

118
00:05:11,081 --> 00:05:11,981
Six.

119
00:05:12,121 --> 00:05:16,386
So v is root six, about two point
four five metres per second.

120
00:05:16,986 --> 00:05:18,526
Here is your recap.

121
00:05:18,526 --> 00:05:20,109
Screenshot this card.

122
00:05:23,309 --> 00:05:25,495
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

123
00:05:25,895 --> 00:05:26,795
One.

124
00:05:26,324 --> 00:05:28,788
What are the two parts
of mechanical energy?

125
00:05:29,688 --> 00:05:30,588
Two.

126
00:05:30,118 --> 00:05:33,517
Why do a light child and a heavy
adult reach the same speed?

127
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:35,317
Three.

128
00:05:34,993 --> 00:05:37,459
When is mechanical energy not conserved?

129
00:05:38,559 --> 00:05:42,474
Next time: press a toy spring
gun, and it fires a ball.

130
00:05:42,474 --> 00:05:44,471
Where was that energy hiding?

131
00:05:44,471 --> 00:05:47,248
Find out in potential energy of a spring.
